  {
   "id": "sec1-1",
   "section": "Background",
   "text": "In October 2019, Bailey co-founded the organization LGB Alliance, an advocacy group which opposes Stonewall's policies on transgender rights.",
   "words": 21,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 7",
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 3",
    "Editor 6",
    "Editor 18"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    13,
    4,
    2,
    1,
    1
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1052011925,
   "revisions": [
    1052011925,
    1027540689,
    1262126126,
    1014024863,
    1111873762
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    13,
    4,
    2,
    1,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-2",
   "section": "Background",
   "text": "She acclaimed the newly formed group on Twitter and said that \"gender extremism is about to meet its match.\"",
   "words": 19,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 7"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    11,
    8
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1027540689,
   "revisions": [
    1027540689,
    1052011925
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    11,
    8
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-3",
   "section": "Background",
   "text": "Her chambers, Garden Court Chambers, announced it would launch an internal investigation after it received complaints alleging transphobia regarding her social media use and her involvement with the LGB Alliance.",
   "words": 30,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 7",
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 4",
    "Editor 19"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    17,
    11,
    1,
    1
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1052011925,
   "revisions": [
    1052011925,
    1027540689,
    1052012173,
    1052107444,
    1151883676
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    16,
    11,
    1,
    1,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-4",
   "section": "Background",
   "text": "She was asked to remove two tweets, one thanking The Times for \"fairly & accurately reporting on the appalling levels of intimidation, fear & coercion that are driving the @stonewalluk trans self-id agenda\" and one stating \"Stonewall recently hired Morgan Page, a male-bodied person who ran workshops with the sole aim of coaching heterosexual men who identify as lesbians on how they can coerce young lesbians into having sex with them.\"",
   "words": 71,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 5"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    71
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1262131081,
   "revisions": [
    1262131081
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    71
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-5",
   "section": "Background",
   "text": "Bailey alleged that Garden Court Chambers and Stonewall were in breach of the Equality Act 2010.",
   "words": 16,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 6",
    "Editor 4",
    "Editor 16"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    10,
    5,
    1
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1051590109,
   "revisions": [
    1051590109,
    1263592754,
    1105594910
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    10,
    5,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec1-6",
   "section": "Background",
   "text": "She claimed victimisation and discrimination on the grounds of sex and/or sexual orientation, and gender-critical philosophical belief against Garden Court, and that Stonewall instructed, caused or induced that unlawful conduct.",
   "words": 32,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 6",
    "Editor 4",
    "Editor 20"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    26,
    5,
    1
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1051590109,
   "revisions": [
    1051590109,
    1263592140,
    1051591724,
    1178722336
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    25,
    5,
    1,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-1",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "The hearing of Bailey's employment tribunal case began on 25 April 2022, considering a number of claims against Garden Court Chambers and against Stonewall.",
   "words": 25,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 4",
    "Editor 12"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    12,
    12,
    1
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1084925125,
   "revisions": [
    1084925125,
    1100915359,
    1262127219
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    12,
    12,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-2",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "The tribunal's decision was published in July 2022.",
   "words": 9,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 4"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    9
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1100765849,
   "revisions": [
    1100765849
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    9
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-3",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "In terms of the claims against Garden Court Chambers, the tribunal ruled in favour of her claim that Garden Court Chambers had discriminated against her by tweeting that complaints against her tweets would be investigated.",
   "words": 35,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 6"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    28,
    7
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1100915359,
   "revisions": [
    1100915359,
    1100763109,
    1100735588,
    1100763308,
    1100916054
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    13,
    12,
    7,
    2,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-4",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "It also ruled in favour of her claims that Garden Court Chambers had discriminated against her and victimised her by concluding in that investigation that two of her tweets had potentially breached the core duties of barristers.",
   "words": 37,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    37
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1100916054,
   "revisions": [
    1100916054,
    1100915359,
    1100763109
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    19,
    11,
    7
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-5",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "One of the tweets was about the concept of a \"cotton ceiling\" and the other regarded her belief that Stonewall has a dangerous agenda regarding gender self-identification.",
   "words": 28,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 4",
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    18,
    10
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1100766703,
   "revisions": [
    1100766703,
    1100916054,
    1100779161
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    18,
    9,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-6",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "She was consequentially awarded £22,000 in damages for injury to feelings.",
   "words": 12,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    12
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1100763109,
   "revisions": [
    1100763109
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    12
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-7",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "The tribunal ruled against her other claims against Garden Court Chambers, ruling that she had not lost income or work opportunities due to the complaints, nor that that Garden Court Chambers had a systemic policy of treating gender-critical beliefs as bigoted.",
   "words": 42,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 4"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    37,
    5
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1100763109,
   "revisions": [
    1100763109,
    1100915359,
    1100744901
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    24,
    13,
    5
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-8",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "The tribunal ruled against all her claims against Stonewall, ruling that Stonewall did not influence the complaints procedure or the policies of Garden Court Chambers.",
   "words": 25,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 1"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    25
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1100763109,
   "revisions": [
    1100763109,
    1100915359,
    1100763308
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    13,
    11,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec2-9",
   "section": "Employment tribunal",
   "text": "In July 2023, the employment tribunal ordered Garden Court Chambers to pay £20,000 legal costs to Bailey because of its \"unreasonable conduct\" during the case.",
   "words": 26,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 10"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    26
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1164290758,
   "revisions": [
    1164290758
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    26
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec3-1",
   "section": "Employment Appeal Tribunal",
   "text": "Bailey appealed against the ruling on the claims against Stonewall.",
   "words": 10,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 11",
    "Editor 4"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    8,
    2
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1112191511,
   "revisions": [
    1112191511,
    1112191642,
    1236775997
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    4,
    4,
    2
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec3-2",
   "section": "Employment Appeal Tribunal",
   "text": "The appeal was heard by the Employment Appeal Tribunal in May 2024, and the appeal was dismissed in July 2024.",
   "words": 20,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 3",
    "Editor 4",
    "Editor 1",
    "Editor 6",
    "Editor 17"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    11,
    5,
    2,
    1,
    1
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1262126126,
   "revisions": [
    1262126126,
    1262178700,
    1027540689,
    1014024863,
    1110929848
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    11,
    5,
    2,
    1,
    1
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec4-1",
   "section": "Court of Appeal",
   "text": "In December 2024, the Court of Appeal granted Bailey permission to appeal the Employment Appeal Tribunal's decision, as ordered by Rt Hon Lord Justice Singh.",
   "words": 26,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 2",
    "Editor 14"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    23,
    3
   ],
   "author_sanctioned": false,
   "sanctioned_words": 0,
   "added_revision": 1262432342,
   "revisions": [
    1262432342,
    1262474240
   ],
   "revision_words": [
    23,
    3
   ],
   "added_before_sanction": null,
   "sanctioned_words_before": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_after": 0,
   "sanctioned_words_during": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "sec4-2",
   "section": "Court of Appeal",
   "text": "In giving permission for the appeal, Lord Justice Singh said, \"The grounds have a real prospect of success but, in any event, raise issues of some general importance which should be considered by this court.",
   "words": 35,
   "authors": [
    "Editor 2",
    "Editor 21"
   ],
   "author_words": [
    34,
    1
   ],
